    "constraints": [
      "Cinnamon build, functional and memory gates first. Fix/reject failures before building/testing GNOME or KDE. After Cinnamon passes, sibling gates may run in parallel.",
      "Preserve resident tray, all tray menu actions/notifications/late-host registration, native fonts/dialogs and the existing on-demand Qt Widgets views.",
      "Preserve all capture/clipboard/shortcuts, live transparent region background, history/configuration/secrets, CLI/MCP authorization and ongoing-operation behavior.",
      "No new packages/cloud machines or separate model dollar cap; ordinary model cost unavailable.",
      "No permanent hidden graphical helper; count the whole family, RSS/PSS/private separately.",
      "Several compatible changes may be combined; save standalone versus integrated pairings, never sum deltas from different baselines.",
      "Keep existing native Unix IPC unless independent attribution justifies a change; preserve its bounded ownership/build/epoch checks.",
      "Next executable locating gate is native StatusNotifier/menu compatibility and memory on actual Cinnamon. Bare Core locator is not product parity.",
      "Final kept candidate needs two independent frozen cold measurements plus native functionality and post-use/lifecycle checks; real guest output remains VNC visible.",
      "Both confirmed closed-family RSS and a five-minute cold peak must meet 40 MiB; cold CPU <0.5% of one core. Keep only measured >1MiB whole-family saving. Native tray/menu and full four-action acceptance are separate mandatory keep gates."
    ],
